~ math is written in AsciiMath inside a raw @@math node, so _, ^, /, and
~ ( ) pass through verbatim. @@math ... math@@ is inline; @@mathblock ...
~ mathblock@@ is a centered display equation. both render to MathML.

Mass and energy are related by @@math E = mc^2 math@@, and the golden
ratio is @@math phi = (1 + sqrt 5)/2 math@@.

~ a display equation — the quadratic formula
@@mathblock x = (-b +- sqrt(b^2 - 4ac))/(2a) mathblock@@

~ a sum, with sub/superscripts and a fraction
@@mathblock sum_(i=1)^n i = (n(n+1))/2 mathblock@@

~ the (engine ...) parameter selects the input syntax; asciimath is the
~ default, so this equation is the same as leaving the parameter off.
@@math(engine asciimath) int_0^1 x^2 dx = 1/3 math@@
